The only reference I've ever seen to rothes was in AD&D's Fiend Folio Tome.
Rothes were basically the "cattle of the caves"; subterranean cultures raised
them for food, but sometimes they might be found wild.  Kinda smaller than
your average cow, from what I remember.

Titanotheres are an extinct mammalian species from the early Cenozoic Era,
quite real.  They resemble rhinoceri more than anything else, but were
substantially larger; they'd be to modern-day rhinoceri what woolly mammoths
were to elephants.  Titanothere means "thunder beast", by the way.

